# Cross-origin isolation: the page may then use SharedArrayBuffer, which the
# multi-core converter (vendor/occt-import-js/mt/) needs for its threads.
# Everything the page loads is its own, so nothing else is affected; without
# these headers the viewer converts on one thread.
# nosniff: a file is only ever run as the type it is served as. (The page's
# Content-Security-Policy is a <meta> in index.html, so the viewer is held to
# it wherever it is served; framing stays open for ?embed=1.)
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
